{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["The meaning of והפשתה והשעורה נכתה: this one [Pharaoh] would not turn back, nor would I pray to heal them [the crops]. And behold, the reason is before you fear and acknowledge and say, 'HaShem is righteous' — the flax and the barley were already struck. And this vav is correct in the language of Ishmael, as I have mentioned. And in my opinion, a word is missing: 'Before I spread [the locusts] as you fear HaShem, you and your servants' — and this is the way of admonition. And the meaning is: when the plague ceases, you rebel. Therefore it is written after it, ויכבד לבו הוא ועבדיו (Exodus 9:34), and its like is not found anywhere else." "<b>והפשתה והשעורה.</b> Scripture reports what happened, and it is clarified from the word נֻכָתָה and also נֻכו (verse 32) that the root of מכה is נכה, like ושֻפו עצמותיו לא רֻאו (Job 33:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The argument is compressed; 'before I spread' likely refers to the threat of locusts in 10:4–5. A word is understood as missing from the biblical text, per Ibn Ezra's reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:07.833002028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}